{
  "id": "08-common-words",
  "title": "The common words",
  "goal": "The words you type most are briefs: short, memorised, often one or two keys. Learn them by frequency, ten at a time.",
  "blocks": [
    { "t": "h", "x": "Why briefs" },
    { "t": "p", "x": "A **brief** is a word's outline taken from Plover or Lapwing, or the cheapest one lyk's rules can find. It is free to be a pure shortcut with no phonetic link to its word. [[it|T]] is just `T`, [[the|-T]] is the right-hand `T`, [[a|A]] is `A`." },
    { "t": "note", "kind": "rule", "x": "Every word has one primary outline. Speed is measured on the fastest outline of each word. Extra outlines never take a stroke another word needs, so what you learn here is never overwritten." },
    { "t": "h", "x": "The smallest words" },
    { "t": "table", "head": ["Word", "Stroke", "Word", "Stroke", "Word", "Stroke"], "rows": [
      ["{{a}}", "[[a|A]]", "{{he}}", "[[he|E]]", "{{to}}", "[[to|O]]"],
      ["{{it}}", "[[it|T]]", "{{is}}", "[[is|S]]", "{{in}}", "[[in|TPH]]"],
      ["{{the}}", "[[the|-T]]", "{{of}}", "[[of|-F]]", "{{and}}", "[[and|SKP]]"],
      ["{{be}}", "[[be|-B]]", "{{for}}", "[[for|-R]]", "{{are}}", "[[are|R]]"],
      ["{{was}}", "[[was|-Z]]", "{{you}}", "[[you|U]]", "{{with}}", "[[with|W]]"],
